# Repository Workflow

[GitHub Issues](https://github.com/th3raid0r/u-forge.ai/issues) is the source of
truth for work, audit findings, and unresolved design decisions. Keep scope,
acceptance criteria, and decisions on the issue; put implementation evidence
on the linked PR. Do not create a parallel backlog or audit ledger in the
checkout (including `.plans/`). Durable implementation contracts belong in
architecture and subsystem docs.

Get the assigned work's scope and acceptance criteria from its GitHub issue,
latest decisions, and linked PRs. A triage or design issue is not authorization
to implement. The harness owns assignment, dispatch, and workflow transitions;
workers do not manage a queue. The implementation worker runs the relevant
local Make checks from [BUILD.md](../BUILD.md) and records results and gaps
against the verified PR head. There is no separate local-checker phase.

## Review and merge signals

- A non-draft PR **with** the `ready for review` label signals automated
  review to the harness. Neither the label alone nor leaving draft alone is
  sufficient. Review applies to the candidate that was checked.
- Adding `ready for merge` to the final, reviewed, non-draft PR opts in to
  hosted CI. It does not approve or authorize a merge. Do not apply it while
  the PR is a draft or while changes are still expected.

## Hosted CI gate

[.github/workflows/ci.yml](../.github/workflows/ci.yml) ignores changes limited
to `.md` and `.mdc` files. For other changes (including `.rules`), only the
first application of `ready for merge` is eligible. The gate checks label
history and verifies that the PR is still open, non-draft, labeled, and on the
same head and base before starting build work. Pushes, relabels, and manual
reruns do not start another build. A failed or stale run is not evidence for
a merge; surface it to the maintainer instead of trying to rearm the gate.

Hosted CI runs the Make format, workspace, strict lint, and
[graph-only test gates](testing-debugging.mdc#canonical-suites). It sets
`UFORGE_SKIP_EMBEDDED_LEMONADE=1` for the whole job so earlier Cargo steps
cannot provision the runtime. Local full verification uses the owned runtime
instead.
